From 88b2ebcd7a1864be16f9799366084fdea4058db2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chai <tsaitomd@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:39:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: lat_write_fp8_paged waits for its producer under
 PDL

0004 added tf_glm_lat_write_fp8_paged and 0006 launches it through cuda_pdl.launch,
but the kernel never opens with glm_pdl::enter(). Every other GLM kernel does, and
TensorFold's own scan says why: a dependent launch may start before the grid before it
retires, so a kernel that reads what that grid wrote has to wait, then read coherently.
Here that grid is the one that writes lat.

It is a correctness fix, not a speed one. On 0001-0016 without this patch,
`zig build test-glm-pdl-scan` fails: "glm_glue_latent.cuh: tf_glm_lat_write_fp8_paged
must open with glm_pdl::enter(); expected 0, found 1". With it, the scan passes
(measured 2026-11-23, CPU only).

It is not part of the fused prompt chunk kernel: every E4M3-page latent write runs it,
decode included, so it is its own patch.

---
 zig/kernels/cuda/glm_glue_latent.cuh | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_glue_latent.cuh b/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_glue_latent.cuh
index f9ebbaf..7db8888 100644
--- a/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_glue_latent.cuh
+++ b/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_glue_latent.cuh
@@ -105,6 +105,7 @@ extern "C" __global__ void __launch_bounds__(512)
 extern "C" __global__ void __launch_bounds__(512)
     tf_glm_lat_write_fp8_paged(const __nv_bfloat16* lat, int64_t stride, unsigned char* cache, float* scales,
                                const int* pos, const int* pt, int64_t ps) {
+  glm_pdl::enter();  // a dependent launch: the kernel before it writes lat
   const int64_t r = blockIdx.x, at = (int64_t)pos[0] + r;
   const int64_t page = (int64_t)pt[at / 512] * ps, row = at % 512;
   const int d = threadIdx.x;
